125	// THE TRANSITION AS DATA (#1374). The side effects were a straight line of
126	// `await api.…` calls, which silently made REST the only way to perform them —
127	// and the sessions `invoke.mjs` hands work to have no REST route to their own
128	// repository, so the last step of every agentic run was the one step that
129	// environment could not take.
130	//
131	// So the sequence is planned as OPS and executed by whoever can. The planner is
132	// the single source of what a convergence IS; the executors differ only in
133	// transport. The session still supplies nothing but the judgment.
134	//
135	// Removes are granular and unconditional — every spelling of the status being
136	// left, not only the ones this snapshot shows (apply-status.mjs's rule: a member's
